Treat a library as not loaded when dlopen() has no RTLD_NOLOAD.

When epoxy only wants to know whether the application already loaded a
GL library, it calls dlopen() with RTLD_NOLOAD, which returns the library
if it is loaded and does not load it otherwise.  zedBSD's <dlfcn.h> has
no RTLD_NOLOAD (it is an extension, not POSIX).  Without it, such a query
now answers that the library is not loaded.  A library epoxy loaded
itself is still found, because its handle is kept; GTK reaches EGL only
through epoxy.  Systems with RTLD_NOLOAD are unchanged.

--- a/src/dispatch_common.c
+++ b/src/dispatch_common.c
@@ -314,10 +314,17 @@
     pthread_mutex_lock(&api.mutex);
     if (!*handle) {
         int flags = RTLD_LAZY | RTLD_LOCAL;
+#ifdef RTLD_NOLOAD
         if (!load)
             flags |= RTLD_NOLOAD;
 
         *handle = dlopen(lib_name, flags);
+#else
+        /* Without RTLD_NOLOAD (zedBSD) a library cannot be looked up without
+         * loading it, so one epoxy has not loaded itself counts as absent. */
+        if (load)
+            *handle = dlopen(lib_name, flags);
+#endif
         if (!*handle) {
             if (exit_on_fail) {
                 fprintf(stderr, "Couldn't open %s: %s\n", lib_name, dlerror());
